MID_SE_Kai_Dit_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Kai_Dit_B_001: Raah!
MID_SE_Kai_Dit_B_002: Trifling. Weak.
MID_SE_Kai_Dit_B_003: {SetColor=Gray}Dietrich's amazing. He cut the enemy clean in half in\na split second.{SetColor=Default}
MID_SE_Kai_Dit_B_004: {SetColor=Gray}He slices through his rivals just as easily as when we\nfought together in the Heroic Games.{SetColor=Default}
MID_SE_Kai_Dit_B_005: Dietrich, you have to teach me that move.
MID_SE_Kai_Dit_B_006: Move? There is no "move." I cut down what\nimpedes me.
MID_SE_Kai_Dit_B_007: O-oh, right. Well, then...how about teaching me your\ntraining routines?
MID_SE_Kai_Dit_B_008: You must be doing some special training, right?\nWhatever it takes, I'm sure I can keep up.
MID_SE_Kai_Dit_B_009: You should have seen the way my pop trained me.\nI've got stamina to spare.
MID_SE_Kai_Dit_B_010: And Bertrand taught me how to use a sword.
MID_SE_Kai_Dit_B_011: If the White-Maned Demon tutored you, you\nmay survive.
MID_SE_Kai_Dit_B_012: If you are unafraid to die, then we may begin.
MID_SE_Kai_Dit_B_013: You think there's a chance I might not make it?\nHey, wait up!
MID_SE_Kai_Dit_B_014: Whew, you're fast. This must be endurance training.\nOr a leg workout.
MID_SE_Kai_Dit_B_015: What you say makes no sense. We have yet to begin.
MID_SE_Kai_Dit_B_016: What do you mean by—*gasp* A rock!
MID_SE_Kai_Dit_B_017: Hah!
MID_SE_Kai_Dit_B_018: Clean in half. If you hadn't cut it, I'd have been in\nbig trouble.
MID_SE_Kai_Dit_B_019: Next, you try. Be sure to affix earplugs and\na blindfold.
MID_SE_Kai_Dit_B_020: Wait. What? Train with my eyes and ears covered?
MID_SE_Kai_Dit_B_021: This training will sharpen your perception. Rocks do\nnot lust for blood, and are therefore suitable.
MID_SE_Kai_Dit_B_022: Once I slept in wolf-infested wilds, but their slavering\npresence woke me easily. It was poor training.
MID_SE_Kai_Dit_B_023: To sharpen yourself, you must balance on the knife's \nedge. If you die, death was inevitable.
MID_SE_Kai_Dit_B_024: I've trained with rocks before, but risking my life to\ntrain? That's new.
MID_SE_Kai_Dit_B_025: We will begin. If you lack the spirit, leave.
MID_SE_Kai_Dit_B_026: I'll do it! This recklessness is strange, but...\noddly familiar.
MID_SE_Kai_Dit_B_027: The wind has grown cold. Shall we end this? Do\nyou live?
MID_SE_Kai_Dit_B_028: Y-yeah, I'm good. I couldn't slice all the rocks,\nthough. I had to dodge some of 'em.
MID_SE_Kai_Dit_B_029: But your training methods aren't half bad. You gotta\nteach me more.
MID_SE_Kai_Dit_B_030: Hm. Why not? I appreciate your hunger. I accept.
MID_SE_Kai_Dit_B_031: Great. I don't know exactly what all this means, but\nI'll see you around, Dietrich.
MID_SE_Kai_Dit_B_032: He does have aptitude. He has the capacity to\nbenefit from this.
MID_SE_Kai_Dit_B_033: Were I to train him, he might prove himself worthy.\nHehehe. I would relish it.
MID_SE_Kai_Dit_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Kai_Dit_A_001: Let's go, Dietrich! Hyaah!
MID_SE_Kai_Dit_A_002: It was too soon for us to meet in battle. I will\nput a stop to it.
MID_SE_Kai_Dit_A_003: Ngh! Whoa! It's not over yet!
MID_SE_Kai_Dit_A_004: So you dodged! Good...very good... Continue\nthe dance!
MID_SE_Kai_Dit_A_005: Ngh, too fast! Whoa! Dietrich? Ah!
MID_SE_Kai_Dit_A_006: Hehehahaha! Yes! Dance faster! Dance beautifully!
MID_SE_Kai_Dit_A_007: Have you lost the will to dance? Then I would see\nyour blood blossom!
MID_SE_Kai_Dit_A_008: Whoaaa!
MID_SE_Kai_Dit_A_009: How long do you intend to lie there?
MID_SE_Kai_Dit_A_010: You caught me off guard! You really meant to kill me\njust now, didn't you?
MID_SE_Kai_Dit_A_011: I was following my instincts. And I was able to\nrestrain them.
MID_SE_Kai_Dit_A_012: In the past, I would have gutted you without\nhesitating and searched for a stronger opponent.
MID_SE_Kai_Dit_A_013: Or I may simply have left your corpse where it lay\nand continued to train.
MID_SE_Kai_Dit_A_014: Dietrich, why are you so desperate for battle?\nAnd strength?
MID_SE_Kai_Dit_A_015: This sword and I are much the same. I constantly\nhone my edge, my reason for being.
MID_SE_Kai_Dit_A_016: You mean it just comes naturally?
MID_SE_Kai_Dit_A_017: Not exactly... The impulse that animates me stems\nfrom a curse laid upon my bloodline.
MID_SE_Kai_Dit_A_018: To give myself to it, to dance with blade in hand,\nis a rapture I cannot resist.
MID_SE_Kai_Dit_A_019: You and I are very different. I train and fight to\nprotect the ones I love.
MID_SE_Kai_Dit_A_020: I do lack this feeling you describe. But I have come to\nunderstand it a little.
MID_SE_Kai_Dit_A_021: Yeah? How?
MID_SE_Kai_Dit_A_022: Since coming here, I have met some who wish to\nstay by my side, and learned from them.
MID_SE_Kai_Dit_A_023: They met a need within me. It is thanks to them, I\nthink, that I spared you.
MID_SE_Kai_Dit_A_024: Maybe we're not so different then. Anyway, I'm not\nas scared of you as I was before.
MID_SE_Kai_Dit_A_025: My essence has not changed. My pursuit of\nstrength continues.
MID_SE_Kai_Dit_A_026: I gotta get stronger for the people I care about.\nNext time I'll beat you.
MID_SE_Kai_Dit_A_027: Oh, then you wish to continue the dance? Step lively!
MID_SE_Kai_Dit_A_028: Hey, "next time" means "next time."